MODULE: GenerationsReclaimedOnlyFirst
TARGET: GenerationsReclaimed
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: reclamation only ever deletes the initial generation, so a later superseded generation leaks
PERTURBS: Reclaim

--- FIND
    /\ \E g \in gens \ {active} : gens' = gens \ {g}
--- REPLACE
    /\ \E g \in (gens \ {active}) \cap {0} : gens' = gens \ {g}
--- END
